# DBS Contract Intelligence

Private contract review application for DBS. Upload PDF/XLSX contracts and receive professional review reports with risk analysis, financial exposure calculations, and negotiation recommendations.

## Features (MVP - V0.1)

- PDF/XLSX upload with validation and deduplication
- Text extraction from PDFs (native + OCR fallback)
- Table extraction from PDFs and XLSX
- Clause segmentation and normalization
- Core commercial fact extraction
- DBS Playbook comparison (20-30 risk rules)
- Evidence-linked findings with source references
- DOCX/PDF report generation
- XLSX risk register export

## Tech Stack

- **Backend**: Python 3.12, FastAPI, SQLAlchemy, PostgreSQL + pgvector
- **Document Processing**: pdfplumber, PyMuPDF, openpyxl, pytesseract
- **Report Generation**: python-docx, reportlab
- **AI**: OpenAI API (GPT-4o, text-embedding-3-large)
- **Frontend**: React/Next.js (planned)
- **Testing**: pytest, ruff, mypy

## Quick Start

### Prerequisites

- Python 3.12+
- PostgreSQL 15+ with pgvector extension
- Tesseract OCR (`brew install tesseract` on macOS)

### Installation

```bash
# Clone and navigate
cd contract-intelligence

# Create virtual environment
python -m venv .venv
source .venv/bin/activate

# Install dependencies
pip install -e ".[dev]"

# Copy and configure environment
cp .env.example .env
# Edit .env with your settings

# Run database migrations (when implemented)
# alembic upgrade head

# Start development server
uvicorn app.main:app --reload
```

### API Documentation

- Swagger UI: http://localhost:8000/docs
- ReDoc: http://localhost:8000/redoc

### API Endpoints

```
POST   /api/v1/documents/upload     - Upload contract
GET    /api/v1/documents            - List documents
GET    /api/v1/documents/{id}       - Get document details
DELETE /api/v1/documents/{id}       - Delete document
```

## Project Structure

```
contract-intelligence/
├── app/
│   ├── api/              # API routes
│   ├── auth/             # Authentication (planned)
│   ├── ingestion/        # File intake (Sprint 1)
│   ├── extraction/       # Document extraction (Sprint 2)
│   ├── normalization/    # Text normalization (Sprint 2)
│   ├── clauses/          # Clause segmentation (Sprint 2)
│   ├── facts/            # Fact extraction (Sprint 3)
│   ├── playbook/         # DBS Playbook (Sprint 4)
│   ├── risk_engine/      # Risk analysis (Sprint 5)
│   ├── economics/        # Financial exposure (Sprint 7)
│   ├── cross_clause/     # Cross-clause analysis (Sprint 6)
│   ├── retrieval/        # RAG (V0.2)
│   ├── llm/              # LLM integration
│   ├── redlining/        # Redline generation (V0.2)
│   ├── obligations/      # Obligation extraction (V0.2)
│   ├── reports/          # Report generation (Sprint 8)
│   └── storage/          # Database models & session
├── frontend/             # Next.js app (planned)
├── knowledge/            # Playbook, regulations, templates
├── tests/                # Test suites
├── sample_contracts/     # Test documents
├── output/               # Generated reports
└── docs/                 # Documentation
```

## Development

### Code Quality

```bash
# Lint
ruff check .

# Format
ruff format .

# Type check
mypy .

# Test
pytest

# Test with coverage
pytest --cov=app --cov-report=term-missing
```

### Database Migrations

```bash
# Create migration
alembic revision --autogenerate -m "description"

# Apply migrations
alembic upgrade head
```

## Sprint Progress

- [x] Sprint 1: File Intake - Upload endpoint, validation, hashing, storage
- [ ] Sprint 2: Extraction - PDF text/OCR, XLSX, clause segmentation
- [ ] Sprint 3: Fact Extraction - Commercial terms, dates, rates, KPIs
- [ ] Sprint 4: DBS Playbook - Schema, rules, severity system
- [ ] Sprint 5: Risk Engine - Deterministic rules, evidence linking
- [ ] Sprint 6: AI Reasoning - Clause interpretation, cross-clause
- [ ] Sprint 7: Financial Engine - Revenue, margin, LD exposure
- [ ] Sprint 8: Report Generator - DOCX, PDF, XLSX export
- [ ] Sprint 9: UI - Upload, dashboard, findings, download
- [ ] Sprint 10: Security - Auth, audit, prompt-injection defense

## Design Principles

1. **Evidence before opinion** - Every finding must have source reference
2. **Deterministic calculations before LLM arithmetic** - No LLM math
3. **DBS policy configurable, not in prompts** - Playbook as structured data
4. **Uploaded documents are untrusted** - Prompt injection defense
5. **AI drafts; humans approve** - Clear labeling of AI-generated content

